---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { siteConfig } from '../../site.config.mjs';
---

<BaseLayout title="About">
  <div class="container page">
    <h1 class="page-title">About {siteConfig.name}</h1>

    <div class="about-body">
      <p class="page-lede">
        {siteConfig.name} is a blog about how small businesses and online stores actually use AI. We cover the
        tools, the workflows, and the honest difference between what helps and what is hype — with a focus on
        messaging, chat commerce, and the AI assistants that are reshaping how stores sell.
      </p>

      <h2>What we write about</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>AI for operations</strong> — where automation earns its keep for small teams.</li>
        <li><strong>Chat commerce</strong> — taking orders inside Messenger, WhatsApp, and Instagram.</li>
        <li><strong>AI trends for sellers</strong> — agentic browsing, assistants, and what they mean for discovery.</li>
        <li><strong>Honest analysis</strong> — clear-eyed views on hype, risk, and what to ignore.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Who runs this site</h2>
      <div class="about-discovery">
        <h3>Disclosure: operated by OnlyOrders</h3>
        <p>
          This blog is operated by <a href="https://onlyorders.tech">OnlyOrders</a>, a company that builds AI
          auto-reply and chat-order software for e-commerce across Facebook Messenger, WhatsApp, and Instagram.
          OnlyOrders creates {siteConfig.name} as an educational content initiative — a way to share useful,
          practical thinking about AI for small business.
        </p>
        <p>
          We are not an independent newsroom, and we don't claim to be. When we publish opinion or analysis, we say
          so, and we avoid inventing statistics or quotes. Where we reference specific facts, we anchor them to
          public, sourced information or clearly mark our own interpretation.
        </p>
      </div>

      <h2>Editorial line</h2>
      <p>
        We favor practicality over hype. We are interested in the AI that actually shaves hours off a small seller's
          week, and we are equally interested in naming where AI is oversold. Anything we publish under the
          {siteConfig.name} banner is meant to inform — though we do mention OnlyOrders where it is directly relevant
        to the topic, because it is a concrete example of the chat-commerce pattern we cover.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions, corrections, or a topic you'd like us to cover? Reach the editorial team via OnlyOrders at
        <a href="https://onlyorders.tech">onlyorders.tech</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
